      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add disableBoundaryAwareCache compat option for prefix-matching prompt cache providers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nDeepSeek and Xiaomi use prefix-matching prompt caching: the system prompt prefix must stay byte-identical across requests for cache hits. OpenClaw 6.x boundary-aware caching keeps stable and dynamic prompt sections in the system prompt, so per-turn dynamic suffix text can break provider prefix matching and reduce cache hits.\n\nThis PR adds `disableBoundaryAwareCache`, auto-detected for `deepseek` and `xiaomi`, which keeps the stable prefix in the system message and moves the dynamic suffix into the first user message. It can be overridden with `compat: { disableBoundaryAwareCache: false }`.\n\nCloses #94518. Related: #91018, #90583.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavior addressed: the production transport path (`buildOpenAICompletionsParams`) resolves DeepSeek/Xiaomi compat, preserves the stable system prefix, moves the dynamic suffix to the first user message, respects explicit `false`, and leaves OpenAI models unchanged.\n\nCurrent head verified: `943858ba56`.\n\nThe committed regression tests now cover:\n\n- DeepSeek default: stable prefix remains the system message; dynamic suffix moves to the first user message.\n- DeepSeek override: `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache: false` preserves the normal stripped system prompt behavior.\n- OpenAI unaffected: non-DeepSeek completions models keep existing boundary handling.\n\nFocused terminal output:\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/llm/providers/openai-completions.test.ts\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.8 <repo>\n\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  34 passed (34)\n   Start at  14:35:07\n   Duration  814ms (transform 583ms, setup 160ms, import 534ms, tests 60ms, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 3.32s\n```\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts\n\n RUN  v4.1.8 <repo>\n\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  286 passed (286)\n   Start at  14:35:11\n   Duration  1.02s (transform 358ms, setup 60ms, import 712ms, tests 201ms, environment 0ms)\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 3.48s\n```\n\nLive DeepSeek API cache headers were not tested because no active API key was available. The proof above exercises the production request-building path that determines whether DeepSeek receives a byte-stable system prompt prefix.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
